 364:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** *
 365:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * This function takes the logical EEPROM address and converts it to the actual
 366:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * physical address and writes data there. If wear leveling is implemented, the
 367:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * writing process will use the wear leveling techniques. This is a blocking
 368:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * function and it does not return until the write operation is completed. The
 369:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * user firmware should not enter Hibernate mode until write is completed. The
 370:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * write operation is allowed in Sleep and Deep-Sleep modes. During the flash
 371:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * operation, the device should not be reset, including the XRES pin, a software
 372:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * reset, and watchdog reset sources. Also, low-voltage detect circuits should
 373:C:\Program Files (x86)\Cypress\PSoC Creator\4.4\PSoC Creator\1\LWO3.cydsn\Generated_Source\PSoC4\cy_em_eeprom.c **** * be configured to generate an interrupt instead of a reset. Otherwise, portions
